## Environment gotchas (fill for this machine; delete lines that don't apply)
<!-- Recurring, turn-wasting environment traps. Capture them once so no future session rediscovers them. -->
- **Windows long paths (`MAX_PATH`):** deeply-nested install or repo paths, such as a long shared-drive or
  scratch path, break pip wheels with long headers (TF/torch) and git object reads. Install heavyweight
  wheels into a short root such as `C:\venvs\<name>`, and set `git config --global core.longpaths true`.
- **Python launcher:** use `py -3.x` or the venv's `python`, not `python3`, which is a Windows Store
  stub on many machines.
- **Shared-drive filesystem (Google Drive / OneDrive File Stream):** may not support symlinks or junctions,
  reporting "Incorrect function". Use a copy or sync step instead of a symlink.
